<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abolition of the Ottoman sultanate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1922">1922</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as abolition of the Sultanate, abolished the Sultanate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The abolition of the Ottoman sultanate was the decision of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-national-assembly-of-turkey">Grand National Assembly</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankara">Ankara</a> in 1922 to end the office of sultan. The last sultan, Mehmed VI, left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a> shortly afterwards, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey</a> was proclaimed in 1923. The event marked the formal end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> after more than six centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abolition-of-the-ottoman-sultanate.jpg" alt="Abolition of the Ottoman sultanate" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sultanvahideddin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
